[
  {
    "title": "What is MongoDB?",
    "id": 1,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ MongoBD is an open source, document oriented NoSQL database management system.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Designed for scalability, flexibility and performance in handling unstructured or semi-structured data.",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "What is a document database?",
    "id": 2,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "A document database (also known as document oriented database or a document store) is a database that stores information in documents.",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Difference between SQL and NoSQL.",
    "id": 3,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "SQL:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ SQL databases are relational databases.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ They use structured tables to store data in rows and columns.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Suitable for applications well-defined schemas and fixed data structures.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ E-commerce platform, HR Management system, etc.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Example: MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "NoSQL:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ NoSQL databases are non-relational databases.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ They provide flexibility in data storage, allowing varied data types and structures. ",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Ideal for applications with dynamic or evolving data models.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ It stores data in the form of documents.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ MongoDB uses BSON to query databases.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ CMS, Social media platforms, Gaming platforms.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Example: MongoDB, Cassandra, Redis.",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "MongoDB Terminology.",
    "id": 4,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "Database --> Collections (one or more) --> Documents (one or more)",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Layer 1: Database",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Layer 2: We can have multiple 'Collections'.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Layer 3: Inside Collections we can have multiple 'Documents'.",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "How MongoDB Works?",
    "id": 5,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "Frontend: HTML, CSS, JS, React.js, Next.js",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Backend: Node.js, Express.js, Next.js, Python, PHP",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Database: MongoDB server contacts with Storage Engine to Read/Write Data Files form the database.",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "JSON VS BSON.",
    "id": 6,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ In MongoDB, we write in JSON format only but behind the scene data is stored in BSON (Binary JSON) format, a binary representation of JSON.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ By utilizing BSON, MongoDB can achieve higher read and write speeds, reduce storage requirements, and improved manipulation capabilities, making it well-suited for handling large and complex datasets while maintaining performance efficiency.",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Managing Databases and Collections.",
    "id": 7,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "Commands:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ show dbs",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ use 'database_name'",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.dropDatabase()",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ show collections",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.createCollection('collection-name')",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.collection-name.drop()",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Examples:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ show dbs",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ use students",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.createCollection('data')",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ show collections",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.data.drop()",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.dropDatabase()",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Inserting Documents in MongoDB.",
    "id": 8,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "To insert one document at a time:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "db.collection-name.insertOne({",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "field 1: value 1,",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "field 2: value 2,",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "...",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "});",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example: db.data.insertOne({ name: 'Raju', age: 30 })",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "To insert many documents at a time:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "db.collection-name.insertMany([",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "{ field 1: value 1, field 2: value 2 },",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "{ field 1: value 1, field 2: value 2 },",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "...",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "]);",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example: db.data.insertMany([{ name: 'Nehal', age: 21 }, { name: 'Raman', age: 20 }, { name: 'Giresh', age: 22 }])",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "When to use Quotes and when not to?",
    "id": 9,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ Special Characters:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "If a field name contains special characters or spaces, or starts with numeric digits, use of quotes is necessary.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example: db.data.insertOne({ name: 'Raju', age: 30, 'course name': 'Mechanical' })",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Reserved Keywords:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "If a field name is reserved keyword in MongoDB, use quote to distinguish it from reserved keywords.",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Ordered and Unordered Insert.",
    "id": 10,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "When executing bulk write operations, 'ordered' and 'unordered' determines the batch behavior.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Ordered Insert:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Default behavior is ordered, where MongoDB stops on the first error and do not insert data present after error.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "db.<collection-name>.insertMany([ doc1, doc2, ... ]);",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example: ",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "db.collection-name.insertMany([",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "{ name: 'Nehal', age: 21 }, ",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "{ _id: ObjectId('6adc387673c0745672f9950b'), name: 'Raman', age: 20 }, ",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "{ name: 'Giresh', age: 22 }])",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "// As Raman data is already present in database, it will show error to insert.",
        "text": ""
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Unordered Insert:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "When executing bulk write operations with unordered flag, MongoDB continues processing after encountering an error.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "db.<collection-name>.insertMany([ doc1, doc2, ... ], { ordered: false });",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example: ",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "db.collection-name.insertMany([",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "{ name: 'Nehal', age: 21 }, ",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "{ _id: ObjectId('6adc387673c0745672f9950b'), name: 'Raman', age: 20 }, ",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "{ name: 'Giresh', age: 22 }",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "], { ordered: false })",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Case Sensitivity in MongoDB.",
    "id": 11,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ Collection names are case-sensitive.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Field names within documents are also case-sensitive.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.Product.insertOne({ name: 'Raju', age: 27 }); ",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.product.insertOne({ name: 'Nilay', age: 29 });",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Finding Documents in MongoDB.",
    "id": 12,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ find():",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "db.collection_name.find({ key: value })",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example: db.data.find({name: 'Tushar'})",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ findOne():",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "db.collection_name.findOne({ key: value })",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example: db.data.findOne({name: 'Tushar'})",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Importing and Exporting JSON in MongoDB.",
    "id": 13,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ mongoimport jsonfile.json –d database_name –c collection_name",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ mongoimport products.json -d shop -c products",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ mongoimport products.json -d shop -c products --jsonArray",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ mongoexport -d shop -c products -o 'C:\\Program Files\\'",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Here, --jsonArray accepts the import of data expressed with multiple MongoDB documents within a single JSON array.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Limited to imports of 16 MB or smaller.",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Comparison Operators.",
    "id": 14,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ $eq: equal to",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ $ne: not equal to",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ $gt: greater than",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ $gte: greater than equal to",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ $lt: less than",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ $lte: less than equal to",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ $in: contains multiple values in array",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ $nin: not in",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.find({ 'price': { $eq: 699 } });",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.category.find({ price: { $in: [249, 129, 39] } });",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Introduction to Cursors.",
    "id": 15,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ Cursors in MongoDB are used to efficiently retrieve large result sets from queries, providing control over the data retrieval process.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ MongoDB retrieves query results in batches using cursors.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Cursors are a pointer to the result set on the server.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Cursors are used to iterate through query results.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ MongoDB retrieves query results in batches, not all at once.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Default batch size is usually 101 documents.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ This improves memory efficiency and network usage.",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Cursor Methods.",
    "id": 16,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ count()",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ limit()",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ skip()",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ sort()",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "db.products.find({ price: { $gt: 250 } }).count();",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "db.products.find({ price: { $gt: 250 } }).limit(5);",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "db.products.find({ price: { $gt: 250 } }).limit(5).skip(2);",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "db.products.find({ price: { $gt: 1250 } }'.limit(3).sort({ price: 1 });",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "(1) for ascending and (-1) for descending",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Cursor Methods (Caveats).",
    "id": 17,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "1. Performance Implications:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ skip() can be inefficient for large offsets.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Using sort() on large result sets may impact performance.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "2. Use with Caution:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Be caution when using skip() and limit() on large collections.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Consider using indexing to optimize query performance.",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Logical Operators.",
    "id": 18,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ $and",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ $or",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ $not",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ $nor",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ { $and: [ { condition1 }, { condition2 }, ... ]}",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ { field: { $not: { operator: value } } }",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.find({$and: [{'price' : {$gt: 100}}, {'name' : 'Diamond Ring'}]})",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.find({$or: [{'price' : {$gt: 100}}, {'name' : 'Diamond Ring'}]})",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.find({$nor: [{'price' : {$gt: 100}}, {'name' : 'Diamond Ring'}]})",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.find({'price' : {$not: {$eq: 100}}})",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Complex Expressions.",
    "id": 19,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ The $expr operator allows using aggregation expressions within a query.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Useful when you need to compare fields from the same document in a more complex manner.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ { $expr: { operator: [field, value] } }",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.find({ $expr: { $gt: ['$price', 1340] } })",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.sales.find({ $expr: { $lt: [{ $subtract: [ '$quantity', '$price' ]}, '$targetPrice' ]} })",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Elements Operator.",
    "id": 20,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ $exists",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ $type",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ $size",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ { field: { $exists: <boolean>} }",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ { field: { $type: '<bson-data-type>' } }",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ { field: { $size: <array-length> } }",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.find({'price' : {$exists: true}, 'price': {$gt: 1200}})",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.find({'price' : {$type : 'number'}}).count()",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.find({'name' : {$type : 2}}).count()",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.comments.find({'comments': {$size: 2}}).count()",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "BSON Type values.",
    "id": 21,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ 1: Double",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ 2: String",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ 3: Object",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ 4: Array",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ 5: Binary Data",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ 6: Undefined",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ 7: Object id",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ 8: Boolean",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ 9: Date",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ 10: Null",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ 11: Regular Expression",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ 12: JavaScript Code",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Projection.",
    "id": 22,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ db.collection.find({}, { field1: 1, field2: 1 })",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ To include specific fields, use projection with a value of 1 for the fields you want.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ To exclude fields, use projection with a value of 0 for the fields you want to exclude.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ You cannot include and exclude fields simultaneously in the same query projection.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.comments.find({'comments': {$size: 2}}, {'comments': 1, '_id': 0}) //_id is exceptional",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.comments.find({'comments': {$size: 2}}, {'title': 0})",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.comments.find({'comments': {$size: 2}}, {'comments': 1, 'author': 0,  '_id': 0}) //Not possible",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Embedded Documents.",
    "id": 23,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ Query documents inside embedded documents using dot notation.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.collection.find({ 'parent.child' : value })",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.comments.find({'comments.user' : 'Lily'})",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.comments.find({'metadata.views' : {$gt: 1200}})",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.comments.find({'comments.user' : 'Henry', 'metadata.likes' : {$gt: 50}})",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "$all vs $elemMatch.",
    "id": 24,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "1. $all:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "The $all operator selects the documents where the value of a field is an array that contains all the specified elements.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ { <field>: { $all: [ <value1> , <value2> ... ] } }",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.comments.find({'comments.user': {$all: ['Alice', 'Vinod']}})",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "2. $elemMatch:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "The $elemMatch  operator matches documents that contain an array field with at least one element that matches all the specified query criteria.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ { <field>: { $elemMatch: { <query1>, <query2>, ... } } }",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.comments.find({'comments' : {$elemMatch: {'user': 'Vinod', 'text' : 'Thanks for sharing.'}}})",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.comments.find({'comments' : {$elemMatch: {'user': 'Vinod', 'text' : 'Thanks for sharing.'}}}, {'comments' : 1})",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "updateOne().",
    "id": 25,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.collectionName.updateOne( { filter }, { $set: { existingField: newValue, newField: 'new value', // ... }, })",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.updateOne({'_id': ObjectId('64c2363be32f4a51b19b9275')}, {$set: {'price' : 45}})",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.updateOne({'name': 'Designer Handbag'}, {$set: {'isFeatured' : true}})",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "updateMany().",
    "id": 26,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.collectionName.updateMany( { filter }, { $set: { existingField: newValue, // ... }, })",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.updateMany({price: 120}, {$set: {'isFeatured': true}})",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Removing.",
    "id": 27,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.collectionName.updateOne( { filter }, { $unset: { fieldName: 1 } } )",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.updateMany({_id: ObjectId('64c2363be32f4a51b19b9275')}, {$unset: {'PrevPrice': 1}})",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.updateMany({'price': {$gt: 10}}, {$unset: {'featured': 1}})",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Rename.",
    "id": 28,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.collectionName.updateOne( { filter }, { $rename: { oldFieldName: 'newFieldName' } });",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.updateMany({'price': {$gt: 10}}, {$rename: {'isFeatured': 'featured'}})",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Updating arrays and Embedded Documents.",
    "id": 29,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "1. Push",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.collectionName.updateOne( { filter }, { $push: { arrayField: 'new element' } });",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.comments.updateOne({_id: 1}, {$push: {comments: {user: 'Prabhas', text: 'Super Star'}}})",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "2. Pop",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.collectionName.updateOne( { filter }, { $pop: { arrayField: value } });",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.comments.updateOne({_id: 1}, {$pop: {comments: 1})  //It willremove last element of array",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Update a field in an embedded document.",
    "id": 30,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.collectionName.updateOne( { filter }, { $set: { 'arrayField.$.text': 'Updated text' } });",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.comments.updateOne({_id: 7, 'comments.user': 'Vinod'}, {$set: {'comments.$.text' : 'Subscribe now.'}})",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Delete Operations in MongoDB.",
    "id": 31,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.collectionName.deleteOne({ filter });",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.sales.deleteMany({ price: 55 });",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.comments.deleteOne({_id: 7})",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.comments.deleteMany({'price': 55})",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "What are Indexes?.",
    "id": 32,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ Indexes are specialized data structures that optimize data retrieval speed in MongoDB.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Indexes store a fraction of data in a more searchable format.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ They enable MongoDB to locate data faster during queries.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Indexes are separate from collections and multiple indexes can exist per collection.",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Benefits of Indexes.",
    "id": 33,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ Faster Querying: Indexes drastically accelerate data retrieval, particularly for large collections.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Efficient Sorting: Indexes facilitate rapid sorting based on specific fields.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Improved Aggregation: Aggregation operations become more efficient with optimized indexes.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Indexing on Multiple Fields: Complex queries can be executed efficiently by utilizing multiple fields in indexes.",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "explain().",
    "id": 34,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ Use explain() method to understand query execution in detail.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.find({ name: 'Air Fryer' }).explain();",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.find({ name: 'Air Fryer' }).explain('executionStats');",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Use it to measure the time taken to execute a query.",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Managing Indexes.",
    "id": 35,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "1. Create Index:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.createIndex({ field: 1 });",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ (1) for storing indexes in ascending order.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ (-1) for storing indexes in descending order.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "2. Get Indexed present:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.collection.getIndexes();",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ _id is a default index.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "3. Delete Indexes:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.collection.dropIndex({ field: 1 });",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.collection.dropIndex( 'index_name' );",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Unique and Text Indexes.",
    "id": 36,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.collection.createIndex({ field: 1 }, { unique: true })",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.collection.createIndex({ field: 'text' });",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.users.createIndex({ email: 1 }, { unique: true })",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "Search in Indexes.",
    "id": 37,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.collection.find({ $text: { $search: 'keyword' } });",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Searching using index is faster than $regex searching.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.find({ field: { $regex: 'air' } })",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "When not to use Indexes?",
    "id": 38,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "1. Indexes on Rarely Used Fields",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Indexing fields that are seldom used in queries can consume unnecessary space and resources..",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "2. Balancing Act",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Indexing requires disk space and memory. Overindexing can lead to resource strain and impact overall performance.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "3. Indexing Small Collections",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ In smaller collections, the cost of index maintenance might outweigh the benefits gained from querying",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "What is Aggregation?",
    "id": 39,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ Definition: Aggregation is the process of performing transformations on documents and combining them to produce computed results.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Pipeline Stages: Aggregations consist of multiple pipeline stages, each performing a specific operation on the input data.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Benefits:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "a. Aggregating Data: Complex calculations and operations are possible.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "b. Advanced Transformations: Data can be combined, reshaped, and computed for insights.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "c. Efficient Processing: Aggregation handles large datasets efficiently.",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "$match.",
    "id": 40,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "The $match stage is similar to the query used as the first argument in .find(). It filters documents based on specified conditions.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ { $match: { <query> } }",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([ { $match: { 'name': 'Sleek Wooden Tuna' } } ])",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "$group.",
    "id": 41,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "The $group stage groups documents by specified fields and performs aggregate operations on grouped data.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "{ $group: {",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "_id: <expression>, // Group key",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "<field1>: { <accumulator1> : <expression1> },",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "...",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "} }",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([{ $group: { _id: '$company', 'Total Products': { $sum: 1 }}}])",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([ { $match: {'price' : { $gt: 1200 } } }, { $group: { _id: '$company', 'Total Products Sum': { $sum: '$price' } } } ])",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.sales.aggregate([ { $match: {'quantity' : 5 } }, { $group: { _id: '$quantity', 'Average': { $avg: '$price' } } } ])",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "$sort.",
    "id": 42,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ { $sort: { <field>: <order> } }",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([ { $sort: { totalProducts: 1 } }])",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([ { $match: {'price' : { $gt: 1200 } } }, { $group: { _id: '$company', 'Total Products Sum': { $sum: '$price' } } }, { $sort: { 'Total Products Sum': -1 } } ])",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ (1) for ascending order and (-1) for descending order.",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "$project.",
    "id": 43,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ The $project stage reshapes documents, includes or excludes fields, and performs operations on fields.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Projects the name field and calculates a discountedPrice field by subtracting 5 from the price.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ $sum, $subtract, $multiply, $avg, etc. are types of expression operator.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Syntax: ",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ { $project: { <field1>: <expression1>, ... } }",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example: ",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([ { $project: { name: 1, discountedPrice: { $subtract: ['$price', 5] } } }])",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([{$project: {'price': 1, '_id': 0}}])",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([{$match: {'price' : {$gt: 1200}}}, {$project: {'price': 1, 'Discount': {$multiply: ['$price', 0.8]}}}])",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "$push.",
    "id": 44,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "The $push stage adds elements to an array field within documents.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ { $push: <expression> }",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([ { $group: { _id: { company: '$company' }, products: { $push: '$name' } } }])",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([ {$match: {'price' : {$gt: 1200}}}, {$group: {_id: '$price', 'All Colors:': {$push : '$colors'}}} ])",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "$unwind.",
    "id": 45,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "The $unwind stage deconstructs an array field and produces multiple documents.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ { $unwind: <array> }",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([ { $unwind: '$colors' }, { $group: { _id: { company: '$company' }, products: { $push: '$colors' } } } ])",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([ {$match: {'price' : {$gt: 1200}}}, {$unwind: '$colors'} , {$group: {_id: '$price', 'All Colors:': {$push : '$colors'}}} ])",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "// Deconstructs the colors array field, groups products by company, and creates an array of colors for each company.",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "$addToSet.",
    "id": 46,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ The $addToSet stage adds elements to an array field while preventing duplicates.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ Groups products by company and creates an array of unique colors for each company.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example: ",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([ { $unwind: '$colors' }, { $group: { _id: { company: '$company' }, products: { $addToSet: '$colors' } } }])",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([ {$match: {'price' : {$gt: 1200}}}, {$unwind: '$colors'} , {$group: {_id: '$price', 'All Colors:': {$addToSet : '$colors'}}}])",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "$size.",
    "id": 47,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ The $size stage calculates the length of an array field.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ { $size: <array> }",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([ { $project: { name: 1, numberOfColors: { $size: '$colors' } } }]);",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([ {$match: {'price' : {$gt: 1200}}}, {$unwind: '$colors'} , {$group: {_id: '$price', colors: {$addToSet : '$colors'}}}, {$project: {_id: 1, colors: 1, 'Color Length': {$size: '$colors'}}}])",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "// Projects the name field and calculates the number of colors in the colors array.",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "$limit and $skip.",
    "id": 48,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ The $limit and $skip stages are useful for pagination, limiting, and skipping results.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ { $limit: <positive integer> }",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([ { $skip: 10 }, { $limit: 10 } ]);",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([ {$match: {'price' : {$gt: 1200}}}, {$unwind: '$colors'} , {$group: {_id: '$price', colors: {$addToSet : '$colors'}}}, {$project: {_id: 1, colors: 1, 'Color Length': {$size: '$colors'}}}, {$skip: 1}, {$limit: 1}])",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "$filter.",
    "id": 49,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ The $filter stage filters elements of an array based on specified conditions.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Syntax: ",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ { $project: { <field>: { $filter: { input: '$<array>’, as: '<variable>’, cond: <expression> }}}}",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.col.aggregate([{ $project: { name: 1, testValues: { $filter: { input:  '$values', as: 'val', cond: {$gt: ['$$val', 30]} } } } }])",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "title": "$addFields.",
    "id": 50,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "▪ The $addFields stage adds new fields to documents in a cleaner way compared to $project.",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Syntax:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ { $addFields: { <field1>: <expression1>, ... } }",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "Example:",
        "text": " "
      },
      {
        "type": "▪ db.products.aggregate([{ $addFields: { discountedPrice: { $subtract: ['$price', 5] } } }])",
        "text": " "
      }
    ]
  },
